WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.810
- All right, let's cap this hour off

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.539
with something uplifting,
this is What I'm Liking.

00:00:04.539 --> 00:00:07.430
(bright upbeat music)

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.210
Best friend, Shawn and Gerard
have set out on a mission

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.420
to get other men to up their kitchen game

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.550
so they can wine and dine their partners.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.620
So they came up with a cooking series

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:17.950
that's in part culinary

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:21.480
and in part reflections on
life and all entertaining.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:24.550
- I wanna know what you
got cooking for right now.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.161
- I got nothing cooking, you gonna cook.

00:00:26.161 --> 00:00:26.994
(Shawn laughs)

00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:29.270
I'm gonna send you home
with a beautiful dessert

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.960
for your wife, a homemade
banana pudding, all right.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.190
- I love that, and I know she will too.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.550
- Yes. One thing that I
always tell everybody,

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.140
it's extremely important,
is you eat with your eyes.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:39.973
You know what I mean?

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.630
You ever had somebody
make like delicious food

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:44.270
and they just kind of
plop it on the plate,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.870
And it's like-
- Yeah, that's me.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.078
(Shawn laughs)
- Right.

00:00:47.078 --> 00:00:48.140
(audience applause)

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.310
- I love these guys so much, y'all,

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.090
that's probably why they were featured

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.280
on Peacock's "Baking It"

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.240
with Maya Rudolph and
Andy Samberg last year,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.073
they're amazing.

00:00:56.073 --> 00:00:57.590
We have them dialed in right now.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.431
What's up Shawn, what's up Gerard.

00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:01.260
(audience applause)

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.690
- Hey Kelly.
- Hey Kelly.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.660
- I mean, I'm just gonna start with this,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.090
if y'all ever wanna send
some banana pudding anywhere,

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:08.760
fine I'll take it.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.730
Anyway, Shawn, tell us more
about how this all got started.

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.350
- Hey Kelly, thanks so much for having us.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.100
Gerard and I've been
friends for about 40 years

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.120
and went to school together,

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.778
we pledged the same frat together-

00:01:20.778 --> 00:01:21.611
- One nine!
(Kelly chuckles)

00:01:21.611 --> 00:01:23.830
- Alpha Phi Fraternity Incorporated,

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.510
and around the time of COVID,

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:29.820
where we needed some COVID
relief, Gerard and I, our wives,

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.990
and a couple of other couples decided

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.640
to have these monthly
rotational dinners, right.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.400
So all of our wives would be
cooking it up in the kitchen

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.310
and having a great time,

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:44.420
and the only guy that
would be doing the cooking

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.350
is Gerard at his house, right.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:51.160
So Trisha, my wife, decided
to come up with a show

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.260
that would bring more guys in the kitchen

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.270
and Gerard would be leading that mission,

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.853
so we're excited about that.

00:01:57.853 --> 00:01:59.870
(audience applause)
- Man, Trisha's a smart woman,

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.710
that's a smart woman.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:04.337
Gerard, what about you,
what made you wanna do this?

00:02:04.337 --> 00:02:06.000
- Oh, I just love cooking,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.980
it's a passion project of mine, honestly.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.860
And frankly, "Foods &amp; Dudes"
is a different kind of show,

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:14.620
it's not your typical cooking show.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:16.290
What we did was take this platform

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.080
and try to do something
a little bit different,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.530
which is have conversations
that most men are not having,

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.980
especially in our community.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.840
We really have to have these
conversations out loud,

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.620
so you'll see on the show, we
talk about education, finance,

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.670
building generational
wealth, raising our children,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.010
relationships, all of those things.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.100
And it's really, really important to us

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.730
to make sure that our viewers

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.920
and everybody gets to see a
different view of black men

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.600
doing something in the home.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.000
We're preparing foods,
we're doing it with love,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.490
basically we're doing it
great, that's the thing.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.441
- Oh my God, those pictures,

00:02:52.441 --> 00:02:54.210
those pictures up, food look so good,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.840
your women are so lucky, oh my goodness!

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.982
All right guys, I'm liking
your post right now.

00:02:58.982 --> 00:03:01.091
(soft bell ring)
(audience applause)

00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:03.860
- Oh thank you, thank
you, oh (indistinct).

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.680
- That's not all, our season long partner,

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.180
Pilot Pen, makers of FriXion,

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.130
the go-to erasable pen at
"The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.500
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.420
just like y'all.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.750
So they're gonna give you
$1,000, $500 for each of you,

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.656
just for being cool.

00:03:16.656 --> 00:03:18.186
(audience applause)

00:03:18.186 --> 00:03:19.706
- Thank you.

00:03:19.706 --> 00:03:21.095
- Now, thank you guys.
- Thank you so much.

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:22.220
- Thank you so much for that.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.080
- [Kelly] Keep it up,
we love watching you,

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.430
you are so funny.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:26.263
And it's so cool

00:03:26.263 --> 00:03:27.960
that you've got a solid
message going as well.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:28.953
Thank you so much.

